<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Dec 18.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Dec 18.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>    Rank		     P/E     Close</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p> 1 Tourism Asset	  3700.00    1.11</p>
<p> 2 Portman Min	     338.10    2.13</p>
<p> 3 Niugini Min	     213.67    2.97</p>
<p> 4 Mayne Nickless	  182.34    8.26</p>
<p> 5 Colonial Coml	   120.77    2.21</p>
<p> 6 Adel Bton Cement	117.39    1.62</p>
<p> 7 Forrestania Gold	 90.68    2.53</p>
<p> 8 Countrywide-PP	   86.86    1.19</p>
<p> 9 Westral Forest	   83.33    2.30</p>
<p>10 Herald Resources	 82.30    0.93</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		1.93    0.84</p>
<p> 2 Consol Rutile	     3.36    0.95</p>
<p> 3 Computer Power	    3.81    3.90</p>
<p> 4 Premier Inv		 4.06    0.72</p>
<p> 5 BTR Plc		     5.59    5.20</p>
<p> 6 Queensland Cotton	 5.75    4.36</p>
<p> 7 Parbury Ltd		 6.08    0.72</p>
<p> 8 Aust Gold Rsc	     6.58    1.20</p>
<p> 9 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.06    0.84</p>
<p>10 RGC			   7.37    5.08</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
